  "notes": "Cash basis village. Governmental lines from the 2022 Total Governmental Funds column (p4-5); fund balances 496,710 -> 675,200 roll forward (p5); transfers 20,000 in (Debt Service) / out (General) from the Total column (p5); proceeds from sale of assets 52,436 = other_financing. Cash: Cash and cash equivalents plus restricted cash from the governmental funds statement (p3; 2021 comparative column for beginning); fund balance also includes due from other funds 226,660 and due from other governments 32,321. Business-type from the cash-basis proprietary statement (p7; disbursements total ties to the Statement of Activities business-type expenses 322,908, p2); interest expense, principal payments and capital outlay printed among nonoperating items recorded as disbursements; proceeds from sale of asset 139 is business_type other_financing; measure cash. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1), Governmental and Business-type columns; totals from the 2022 Total column. Detail: General Fund revenues and other financing from its budget schedule (p8); General Fund expenditures from the departmental combining schedule (p15, more detailed; the p8 object lines are its Total column, not recorded twice). Street, Debt Service, Keno, Water, Sewer, Trash budget schedules p9-14. Zero-actual lines with only a budget (General transfers in 30,000; Street transfers in 100,000; Water miscellaneous 2,200 and transfers out (30,000); Sewer miscellaneous and capital outlay 118,000) not recorded. Intergovernmental lines kept as other state aid (no grantor/program printed). Trash and Keno schedules print no total line for a single-line section. Read pages 1-15 of 15"
}
